@startuml 05-listing-statuses
!include _style.iuml
title Listing statuses

[*] --> DRAFT : host creates listing
DRAFT --> PUBLISHED : host publishes\n(needs at least one room)
PUBLISHED --> PAUSED : host pauses
PAUSED --> PUBLISHED : host resumes\n(needs a room)
PUBLISHED --> DRAFT : last room deleted

state SUSPENDED #FDECEC

DRAFT --> SUSPENDED
PUBLISHED --> SUSPENDED
PAUSED --> SUSPENDED : admin suspends (source ADMIN)\nowner blocked (OWNER_BLOCKED)\nowner deleted account (OWNER_DELETED)

SUSPENDED --> DRAFT
SUSPENDED --> PUBLISHED
SUSPENDED --> PAUSED : restore to statusBeforeSuspension\n(DRAFT if it has no rooms any more)

DRAFT --> [*] : host deletes\n(no active bookings)

note right of SUSPENDED
  Who may lift it depends on the source:
  ADMIN          -> admin "unsuspend" only
  OWNER_BLOCKED  -> unblocking the owner only
  OWNER_DELETED  -> admin restoring the account
                    (purged after 30 days)
  The owner can never publish, pause or resume it.
  Suspending, blocking the owner or deleting is
  refused (409) while the listing has active bookings.
  The host may delete a listing (any status) when it
  has no active bookings.
end note
note left of PUBLISHED
  Only PUBLISHED listings are visible.
  GET /api/v3/listings/{id} answers 404
  to everyone except the owner and admins.
end note
@enduml
